  "fidelity": {
   "functional": null,
   "timed": null,
   "electrical": {
    "claims": "The triac primitive (SPEC-004): off it leaks the datasheet's maximum 10 uA at VDRM; it turns on when its gate current reaches the maximum trigger current of the quadrant it is in (5, 5, 5, 7 mA), its gate a junction to MT1 at the typical 0.66 V; on, it drops the maximum 1.9 V at 0.85 A and holds down to the typical 1.5 mA. Fixtures in the datasheet's test circuit (12 V, 100 ohm) for each quadrant's trigger, latching, dropping out below the holding current, blocking at VDRM and the 0.1 V non-trigger gate voltage.",
    "omissions": [
     "breakover: set 25 % above the rated VDRM (${vbo} V); the datasheet gives only the rating",
     "the trigger currents at their maxima: a real part triggers at less; and the latching current (above the holding current)",
     "the commutating dV/dt (5 V/us) and the static dv/dt: neither false triggering nor failure to turn off with an inductive load",
     "turn-on time (2 us typical) and the on-state curve beyond its 0.85 A point",
     "temperature: the trigger currents double at -40 C",
     "surge and I2t ratings and damage",
     "device-to-device spread",
     "no manufacturer model qualification"
    ],
    "validation": [
     "tests/*.json"
    ]
   }
  },
  "provenance": {
